  "note": "Oudezijds Achterburgwal 175, 177 and 179 (odd side): a 17th-c. brick front (1626) over a tall white pilastered ground storey, its cornice broken by a raised centre with an arched light and a carved crest; a 1905 red-brick front with segmental windows, a white console entablature, a pedimented dormer and a striped basement of three round arches; and a plastered 1697 front with a white cornice and a red-tiled roof with one dormer. Run cut out of achterburgwal-167-179."
 },
